# R5-3a (steps/array-receiver-20261011.md): the levels of a nested own Array are made and filled by the source.
# `[]: []: int a 2` is an Array of two descriptor cells; `[]: int row 3` is made where it stands and stored into a
# cell by reference; `a[1]` reads back as that Array -- identity through an untyped `@: void` -- and
# `length(a[1])` is its length; an uncounted `int: []: []: empty` is constructed empty.  Before: "a nested own Array
# declaration is not built yet".  Natively and with the methods walked.  Entry 7.
fn: work () int
    []: []: int a 2
    []: int row 3
    int: []: []: empty
    row[0]: 9
    if: length(a) != 2U || length(empty) != 0U
        return: 81
    a[1]: row
    if: length(a[1]) != 3U
        return: 82
    @: got void a[1]
    @: rd void row
    if: got != rd
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
